content.text:
Now Main.js. Also loading UI. Let's write.

Main:
- import style.
- renderer lazy.
- Menu instantiated immediately; its preview starts.
- startGame flow with loading overlay:
```
async function startGame(map, skin, quality) {
  if (busy) return;
  busy = true;
  menu.hide();
  showLoading(...);
  await nextFrame(); await nextFrame();
  try {
    if (!renderer) renderer = new THREE.WebGLRenderer({canvas, antialias: !touch, powerPreference:'high-performance'});
    game = new Game({...});
    hide loading
  } catch(e) { show error }
  busy=false;
}
```
But menu.hide disposes preview renderer; if game creation fails, need show menu. Handle.
- Renderer creation antialias: use `matchMedia('(pointer: coarse)').matches ? false : true`; mobile off.
- Loading steps text with timeouts? We can show "Generando mapa..." then create synchronously. Since world creation may block ~200ms, loading appears for one frame. Add a minimum display time of 500ms using setTimeout to let user see; not necessary. Do:
```
showLoading();
setTimeout(create, 120)
```
- On restart: dispose game, hide end, show loading, create new after 80ms.
- On exit: dispose game, hide end/hud, show menu.
- Set body class `playing`.
- Handle WebGL unsupported.
- `loading` title/sub changes.
- Bind `#again-btn` in Game already; Game.opts.onRestart calls main restart.

Need to avoid Game constructor throwing due to DOM not ready; script module at end of body, fine.

`menu.hide()` cancels preview; if returning to menu, `menu.show()` reinit preview.

Potential issue: Menu's preview `initPreview` uses `this.selectedSkin` which is set in bindSkin before initPreview? Constructor order: buildMaps, bindSkin, bindButtons, initPreview. bindSkin sets selectedSkin and calls apply (which references previewChar undefined). Then initPreview uses selectedSkin. Good.

But `applySkin` called in bindSkin before preview exists; it calls `if (this.previewChar)` false. Good.

After returning to menu and recreating preview, the preview uses `this.selectedSkin`; if user changed skin, selectedSkin persists. But `setGloves` applied? createPlayerCharacter(scene, selectedSkin) uses gloves. Weapon set 'pio' always, even if gloves; minor. Set weapon based on skin in initPreview. Fix.

Also after preview re-init, `setGloves` toggling works.

Main `menu.show()` when returning; but if preview renderer disposed, `initPreview` creates new scene and loop. Good.

One more: Game dispose removes scene objects but renderer still points at canvas. Menu background is opaque. Fine.

Let's write Main.

