Now spawn logic and camera. Modify Game.findSpawn to landmark-based and return yaw; player yaw.

Current:
```
const pSpawn = this.findSpawn(55,140);
...
this.player.yaw = Math.random()*2PI;
```
Change findSpawn:
```
findSpawn(minR,maxR,avoid,avoidDist, landmarkBias=true) {
 const landmarks = [{x:95,z:-40},{x:-95,z:35},{x:0,z:0},{x:10,z:105}];
 const lm = landmarks[Math.floor(Math.random()*landmarks.length)];
 for tries:
   const a = random; const r = rand(minR,maxR);
   x = lm.x + cos(a)*r; z = lm.z + sin(a)*r;
   ...
   return {x,z,yaw: Math.atan2(lm.x-x, lm.z-z)}
}
```
But minR/maxR relative to landmark, radius 55-140 could put outside map. Clamp. For player use 55-100 around landmark. For bots use random map around center to spread. Maybe bots use existing radius. Add optional `center` param.

Simpler:
- Player spawn: choose landmark, distance 55-95, valid.
- Bots: random around map center 20-180, as before.
Add method `findLandmarkSpawn()`.

Implement:
```
findSpawn(minR,maxR,avoid,avoidDist=0, center=null) {
 const cx = center?center.x:0, cz=center?center.z:0;
 for ... a,r; x=cx+cos(a)*r; z=cz+sin(a)*r; if hypot>195 continue...
 return {x,z, yaw: center ? Math.atan2(center.x-x, center.z-z) : 0}
}
```
Player:
```
const lm = pick; const pSpawn=this.findSpawn(45,90,null,0,lm); this.player.yaw=pSpawn.yaw
```
Bots:
```
