- The pause button is cut off at top right (only a sliver). HUD top right has minimap 92px and pause button, but viewport 390 wide; match info center overlaps? The pause button is at x ~388? Need fix.
- The health panel bottom left and weapon panel bottom right overlap with touch buttons, especially weapon panel behind fire buttons. The touch controls (right) overlay weapon panel. Need redesign mobile HUD to avoid overlap.
- Joystick at bottom left overlaps health panel (health panel at bottom, joystick above but overlapping its top? It looks joystick sits on health panel). Actually health panel bottom left extends under joystick? The joystick is at left 22 bottom 118, health panel bottom 10 with height ~80, so joystick bottom at 118 from bottom, above health panel. In screenshot, joystick at y~600-700, health panel at y~745-830; no overlap. Good.
- Weapon panel bottom right is at bottom 10, width 47vw (~183), and touch actions right 16 bottom 16 width 196 height 178 -> overlap completely. The touch buttons are on top of weapon panel. Need move weapon panel up or touch actions up/right. On mobile, weapon panel could be moved above the touch controls, e.g., bottom: 200px, right: 10px; width 44vw. But then it may overlap other HUD. Or make touch actions lower/right and weapon panel at bottom center? Better: on mobile, move weapon panel to top-left under feed? Hmm.

Standard mobile BR layout: health bottom-left, weapon info bottom-center/right above fire buttons, minimap top-right, joystick bottom-left, fire button bottom-right. We can set weapon panel bottom: 200px, right: 12px on mobile, and touch actions bottom 16 right 16. But weapon panel height ~100, so it sits above buttons. It may overlap the look zone but that's okay. However the weapon panel is wide 47vw ~183 and at right, it might cover center. Acceptable.

Alternatively shrink touch action cluster and move it up, but it's already 196x178; on 390 width, it occupies right half. Weapon panel could be hidden on mobile (weapon info already in touch UI? Not really). Keep but move up.

- The minimap is 92px and pause button at far right; the pause button is cut because `.hud-right` gap and width? The top row has hud-left (alive + zone) ~180px, match-info ~? center, hud-right minimap 92 + pause 34 + gap = 132. Total >390. Since flex justify-between, items shrink? `.hud-left` ~180, match-info ~60, hud-right 132 = 372 + gaps 20 = 392, just over. The pause button is pushed off-screen. Fix mobile: hide match-info on <=640 (or show only timer small), or make minimap 82 and pause 28. Better: hide `.match-info` on mobile (the map name/timer) or move timer into zone pill. The match timer is less critical; the zone pill shows hazard. But match timer useful. Could place timer in top center absolute small. Simpler: at max-width 640, `.match-info { position:absolute; left:50%; transform:translateX(-50%); }` and hide span, keep b; but it may overlap. Or hide `.match-info span` already, b remains. It's at center and width ~40. The overlap is due to hud-left + hud-right. Reduce minimap to 82 and pause to 30, hide zone pill small? Let's compute: hud-left alive pill ~70 + zone pill ~70 = 146; hud-right minimap 82 + pause 30 + gap 6 = 118; center 40; total 304 + gaps 20 = 324, fits 390. Currently minimap 92, pause 34 => 132, total 338 + gaps = 358, should fit 390. Why cut? Maybe `.hud` padding 12 each => 366 available. Still. The screenshot pause button at x=388 clipped, so something else: `.match-info` maybe width auto but text "LA ZONA DE LA ERUPCIÓN" hidden span, b timer 00:07 ~50. hud-left ~174. 174+50+132=356, fits 366. Hmm maybe hud-left is wider due to zone pill "LAVA 1:53" ~80 and alive ~85 => 165. Still. Maybe the minimap canvas CSS width 92 but actual element has 118 intrinsic? CSS width 92 applies. The pause button is 34. It might be at x 388 because `.hud-right` is pushed by match-info and gap; justify-content space-between doesn't guarantee fit if sum > width. We can reduce/hide match-info on mobile to be safe. Let's set `.match-info { display:none; }` at max-width 640? But then timer gone. Could integrate timer into zone pill? The zone pill currently shows LAVA + countdown, not match time. Not critical. I'd hide match-info on <=640 to free space. Or move timer to top center above? Hmm.

- The touch UI is shown (we forced). The buttons look okay but weapon panel overlaps.

- The mobile scene at center (0,0) shows a volcano-like orange hill with lava streaks. Wait center 0,0 is near volcano? No, the orange hill is the volcano at z105, 105m away, visible in background. The foreground is green plains with a building. Looks decent. The sky has a huge orange sun glow; nice.

- The FOV/third-person camera at 390x844 shows character large. Fine.

- Health panel width 47vw (~183) and weapon panel 47vw (~183), both fit with gap 6 => 372 + padding 24 = 396, slightly over 390. That's why maybe overlap/clipping. Set widths to 44vw or 45vw. At 390, 44vw=171, two + gap 6 + padding 24 = 372. Good. Set health/weapon width 44vw. Also weapon panel content might wrap.

- Bottom HUD height: health panel ~80; weapon panel ~100; touch actions 178. Moving weapon panel above touch actions: `bottom: 205px` on mobile. But then it overlaps the joystick? Right side only. Fine. However the special button is part of weapon panel, so special button moves up too, away from thumb. Touch special button also exists in touch UI (the ⚡ button at right 98 bottom 64). So the weapon panel's special button is redundant on mobile; but moving panel up means the special button not thumb-reachable, but touch special exists. Good.

Let's adjust mobile CSS:
```
@media (max-width:640px) {
  .health-panel, .weapon-panel { width: 44vw; }
  .weapon-panel { position: absolute; right: max(12px, env(safe-area-inset-right)); bottom: 200px; }
  .match-info { display:none; }
  .hud-right { gap:4px; }
  #minimap { width:84px; height:84px; }
  .icon-btn { width:30px; height:30px; }
  .feed { width: 58vw; }
  .killfeed { top: 150px; width: 52vw; }
}
```
But `.hud-bottom` is flex with health and weapon panels. If we make weapon panel position absolute, it leaves health panel only. `.hud-bottom` justify-content space-between with one child left; fine. But absolute positioning relative to `.hud` (position absolute inset 0). Set bottom 200px. The weapon panel is removed from flex. Need to ensure `.hud-bottom` doesn't reserve space; okay.

Alternatively keep in flow and set `.hud-bottom { align-items:flex-start; }` etc. Absolute is easier.

But note `.weapon-panel` bottom 200px on a 844 screen -> y ~540, height 100 -> top 440, which overlaps crosshair area? Crosshair center y=422. It may overlap slightly. Better bottom 190px -> top 450. Crosshair at 422, okay. On smaller phones 640 height, bottom 190 -> top 350, near center. Hmm. Maybe bottom: 170px; touch cluster top at bottom 16+178=194, so 170 is inside cluster. Need at least 200. On 640 height, crosshair 320, weapon top 340. Fine. Use bottom: 205px.

Touch buttons cluster at bottom 16, height 178 => top = 844-16-178=650. Weapon panel bottom 205 => bottom y=639, height ~100 => top 539. Gap 11. Good. On 640 height: cluster top 446, weapon bottom y=435, top 335; crosshair 320; gap 15. Good.

Also `interact-prompt` bottom 26% (219px) may overlap weapon panel; but prompt only near loot. Fine.

- The joystick is bottom 118, height 104 -> top 622. Health panel top ~745. Fine.

- The health panel is 44vw ~171, content fits.

- The mobile HUD top right minimap 84 + pause 30. Good.

- Also hide match-info on mobile frees center.

Let's apply.

